1
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,797
Issy, years ago our village was
wiped out during a monster attack.

2
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:13,497
Lammis and I are among the few people
who managed to survive the destruction.

3
00:00:13,580 --> 00:00:15,639
Both of our parents ended up dying.

4
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:19,097
Lammis had her blessing then,
but she was too scared to act.

5
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:22,877
That's why, to this day, she blames herself
for not being able to save everyone.

6
00:00:22,960 --> 00:00:26,780
I had no idea Lamas went
through such an awful ordeal.

7
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:28,591
She's always so cheerful.

8
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:32,508
Once spring comes, the hunters
will become more active again.

9
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:35,360
Next time, I'll protect Lamas.

10
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:44,060
Hello there!

11
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:47,900
It's freezing out here.

12
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:50,669
I really should have
put on an extra scarf.

13
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:52,700
Yeah, that one looks gaudy.

14
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,317
What are you even talking about?

15
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:55,635
Red's my lucky color.

16
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:56,700
Hello, there.

17
00:00:57,860 --> 00:00:59,742
This stuff always hits the spot.

18
00:00:59,880 --> 00:01:01,977
Is that why you buy the
same thing every day?

19
00:01:02,060 --> 00:01:02,890
What about it?

20
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:05,218
Am I not allowed to have a favorite?

21
00:01:07,340 --> 00:01:08,760
Catch you later, Boxo.

22
00:01:09,140 --> 00:01:10,140
See you tomorrow.

23
00:01:10,520 --> 00:01:11,700
Thank you very much.

24
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:25,597
My skin is red and white and pink glances.

25
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:32,017
I'm hot because I don't know.

26
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:36,417
If you're my skin, I need
you to worry about it.

27
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,997
All of a sudden, let's go!

28
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:43,677
I need you to worry about it.

29
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:45,980
Let's go.

30
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:52,600
When I'm ready, let's go?

31
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:52,637
For real, I wish you could have been
there to see their faces when it happened.

32
00:02:52,720 --> 00:02:54,191
Whoa, what a coincidence.

33
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:57,857
It's funny, I was actually just
about to head over to your shop.

34
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:59,300
Oh, is that so?

35
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:02,756
I had to pick up some things,
but I'm going there too.

36
00:03:04,020 --> 00:03:06,961
Also, I think your scarf
is a really pretty color.

37
00:03:07,260 --> 00:03:09,460
Yeah, I'm partial to red myself.

38
00:03:10,820 --> 00:03:13,277
Be a gentleman and help
her carry her things.

39
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:15,440
You're right, if you don't mind.

40
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:18,379
Thank you so much, you're too nice.

41
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:23,800
Here I am again.

42
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:27,259
I even made sure to dress
up in your favorite color.

43
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:31,300
And yet all I can do is watch
as you walk away. Alright.

44
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:38,377
What's going on? Boxxo?

45
00:03:38,460 --> 00:03:40,360
Is that some kind of vegetable?

46
00:03:41,120 --> 00:03:43,355
Are you saying you want me to take it?

47
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,560
Hello there!

48
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:51,580
Where did these eggs come from?

49
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:58,460
Wait a sec.

50
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:00,180
What's this?

51
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,880
Soup stock, made from flying fish.

52
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,300
What am I supposed to do with this?

53
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:06,700
I don't get it.

54
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:14,057
Do you want me to stew all of
these ingredients together?

55
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:14,970
Hello there.

56
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,660
Thank you so much.

57
00:04:17,120 --> 00:04:19,708
With this, I'll finally
catch his attention.

58
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:23,440
She's super cute!

59
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:26,420
Gorth, Boxxo, love is the best.

60
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:28,288
Every day seems to sparkle.

61
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,200
Oh, yeah. Get this.

62
00:04:30,380 --> 00:04:31,677
She cooked me dinner again.

63
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:33,780
It was so unbelievably good.

64
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:36,730
Huh?

65
00:04:36,813 --> 00:04:37,920
What's this now, Boxxo?

66
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:40,944
Are you giving me one on
the house to celebrate?

67
00:04:41,640 --> 00:04:42,960
Ah! It's hot!

68
00:04:44,060 --> 00:04:46,001
That's what you get for bragging.

69
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:55,560
Hey, Boxo, we're back! Hello there!

70
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:58,320
It's pretty warm today.

71
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:01,129
Why don't we get
something cold and bubbly?

72
00:05:05,180 --> 00:05:10,100
Oh yeah, we're going to be setting out
tomorrow, okay? Hello there! That's right.

73
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:11,740
Time sure flies fast.

74
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:14,317
You'll be traveling with
the Menagerie of Fools.

75
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,230
Uh-huh.

76
00:05:15,313 --> 00:05:18,371
They said something about
checking on the crocodile fiends.

77
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,414
Crocodile fiends, huh?

78
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:22,797
They're one of the three
big monster factions

79
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:25,233
that inhabit the Clearflow Lake stratum.

80
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:28,237
We defeated the frog fiends
and the two-headed snakes.

81
00:05:28,320 --> 00:05:32,177
So all we have to do is make sure
the crocodile fiends don't multiply!

82
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:33,977
It's just going to be a scouting mission.

83
00:05:34,060 --> 00:05:37,236
It's dangerous to let their
population grow unchecked.

84
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:39,077
A king frog fiend popped up.

85
00:05:39,160 --> 00:05:41,360
As well as a giant two-headed snake.

86
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:46,020
I can't help but feel something
strange is going on in this stratum?

87
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:47,230
Promise me.

88
00:05:47,313 --> 00:05:49,640
You'll run away if things get too dicey.

89
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,350
Sure!

90
00:05:51,433 --> 00:05:54,037
Boxo and I'll make a run for
it if it's too much, right?

91
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:54,980
Hello there!

92
00:05:55,740 --> 00:05:56,570
Yeah.

93
00:05:56,740 --> 00:05:59,387
No matter what happens,
I'll keep Lamas safe.

94
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,220
Ah, our guest of honor.

95
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:06,117
Thanks for waiting, everyone.

96
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:08,980
It's Lamas and Boxo! We meet again.

97
00:06:09,240 --> 00:06:12,380
You're a welcome sight.
Both of you. Mm-hmm.

98
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:13,875
Thanks for having us.

99
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:16,040
Hey, Lamas! Boxo! Whoa!

100
00:06:16,520 --> 00:06:19,580
You be careful out there! We will! Right!

101
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:21,300
Time to head out!

102
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:24,860
You two can get on if
you'd like. No, thanks.

103
00:06:25,120 --> 00:06:26,767
I'll walk if you don't mind.

104
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:28,801
It'll be helpful for my training.

105
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:29,850
All right.

106
00:06:29,933 --> 00:06:32,152
That just means there's more room for me.

107
00:06:32,620 --> 00:06:35,580
Wait, you're coming too, Hulemy? Why not?

108
00:06:35,860 --> 00:06:37,213
It's an ecology survey.

109
00:06:37,420 --> 00:06:39,837
You'll need someone who actually
knows what they're doing.

110
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,744
Plus, Director Bear
practically begged me to go.

111
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,697
Did she keep it a secret
so she could surprise us?

112
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:50,677
Well, everything should work out fine
with the menagerie of fools here.

113
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:54,017
This weather's pretty nice.

114
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:55,677
If I'm being honest,

115
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:59,077
I'm not the kind of guy who could spend
his whole life cooped up in a town.

116
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:03,117
I'll waste away if I don't take
a breather outside now and again.

117
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,377
Hello there!

118
00:07:04,460 --> 00:07:07,297
Is anyone else ready for a little break?

119
00:07:07,380 --> 00:07:09,260
I'm starving right now!

120
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:20,620
Um, thanks for that.

121
00:07:20,780 --> 00:07:21,780
Don't mention it.

122
00:07:24,040 --> 00:07:26,557
Well, I don't want to just
sit here and do nothing.

123
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:28,464
Maybe I could throw some rocks.

124
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:29,960
Not a bad idea.

125
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:33,614
That's a good way of putting
her absurd strength to use.

126
00:07:35,220 --> 00:07:36,050
Lammis, hmm?

127
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:40,544
Isn't this one of those
bubbly drinks from Boxo?

128
00:07:40,820 --> 00:07:43,277
But the bottle is a lot harder than usual.

129
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,177
Don't you think he's
telling you to throw it?

130
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:46,260
Oh, you're right.

131
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:54,145
Wow, that got some serious
distance, didn't it?

132
00:07:55,180 --> 00:07:56,010
Come on!

133
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:04,917
I can't believe we get to eat all
this yummy stuff out on a campaign.

134
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,917
They're way better than field rations.

135
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,797
We have Boxxo to thank for that.

136
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:12,517
As long as he's here, or we won't need
to worry about running out of food.

137
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:13,430
Hooray!

138
00:08:13,513 --> 00:08:15,917
We don't have to catch monsters
and roast them whole anymore!

139
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:16,830
Yeah, thank goodness!

140
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:18,171
I'm so happy I could cry!

141
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:22,840
Alright then, if you'll
excuse me. Be careful.

142
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:28,517
Do you have some sort of new
function you want to show us, Boxo?

143
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:29,430
Hello there.

144
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:32,537
Looks like there's something
new on your side there.

145
00:08:32,620 --> 00:08:35,149
Not to mention this
strange foldable chair.

146
00:08:35,580 --> 00:08:37,580
What's the hole in the middle for?

147
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:41,520
Oh, this bag fits perfectly
into the hole in the chair.

148
00:08:41,860 --> 00:08:44,448
All that's left is to
figure out this thing.

149
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:49,817
So we have a tent that's just
big enough for one person

150
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:55,060
and a chair with a hole that perfectly fits
a bag. Wait a second. Is this a toilet?

151
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:57,140
A toilet? Ding, ding.

152
00:08:57,580 --> 00:08:59,597
It's a simple toilet
installed on the sides of

153
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:02,497
vending machines to help
with disaster management.

154
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:03,560
I get it.

155
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:05,577
With this setup, nobody can see you.

156
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:09,013
And once you're done, you can
cleanly dispose of the bag.

157
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:11,100
What a clever idea.

158
00:09:11,400 --> 00:09:12,640
Am I right, Boxo?

159
00:09:12,960 --> 00:09:13,820
Hello there.

160
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:15,740
How convenient.

161
00:09:15,980 --> 00:09:17,020
Ain't I a genius?

162
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:20,357
If I hadn't convinced
Boxo to come with us,

163
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:23,057
you wouldn't have had
all these conveniences.

164
00:09:23,140 --> 00:09:26,020
Go on, tell me how wonderful I am.

165
00:09:26,160 --> 00:09:27,897
You don't get to steal Boxo's credit,

166
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:30,497
and frankly, it's disgusting
you'd even consider it.

167
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:31,410
Ouch.

168
00:09:35,660 --> 00:09:37,697
We're entering monster territory now,

169
00:09:37,780 --> 00:09:40,197
so you guys better stay
on guard for any danger.

170
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:42,217
Then you should keep watch too, Captain.

171
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:43,130
No thanks.

172
00:09:43,213 --> 00:09:45,740
Maybe we should poke
him with a spear. Silly.

173
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:46,980
He deserves it.

174
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:49,106
Could you come down, Captain?

175
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:52,341
We'd like to discuss our
plans for how to proceed.

176
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:54,009
Yeah, yeah, if you insist.

177
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:58,240
Hey, Aka, Shiro, you
two scout the area. Huh?

178
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:00,088
All right, we'll get going.

179
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:02,900
He wants them to handle recon?

180
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:04,818
By all appearances,

181
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:09,607
they look to be more like the life of
the party than responsible party members.

182
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:16,920
Guess that goes to show you shouldn't
judge people by how they look.

183
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:20,917
Might as well kick our feet
back while we wait for them.

184
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,980
Boxxo, you got any tasty snacks?

185
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:25,217
I'd like some sweetened tea, please.

186
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:26,130
Hello there!

187
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:29,680
We're back, boss!

188
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:31,320
You miss us?

189
00:10:31,660 --> 00:10:32,778
Good work, you two.

190
00:10:33,420 --> 00:10:35,697
Take a break, then let's hear your report.

191
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:36,610
Yes, sir.

192
00:10:39,940 --> 00:10:40,770
Let's see.

193
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:43,877
I think it was about two hours
northeast of here, right, Aka?

194
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:45,397
That's exactly right, Shiro.

195
00:10:45,480 --> 00:10:49,186
We found a small marsh with nearly
30 of them splashing around.

196
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:50,720
30 of them, huh?

197
00:10:50,980 --> 00:10:53,617
How big do groups of these
fiends typically get?

198
00:10:53,700 --> 00:10:55,940
They number from 10 to 50 at the most.

199
00:10:56,300 --> 00:10:58,480
I'd say 30 makes it an average group.

200
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,657
How tall would you say they were?

201
00:11:00,740 --> 00:11:01,920
Let me think.

202
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:05,120
On their hind legs, maybe
about as tall as us?

203
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,940
Yeah, give or take a bit.

204
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:09,069
That's smaller than usual.

205
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:13,397
Have they been short on food since they
can no longer attack the frog fiends?

206
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:15,557
But I thought the
crocodile fiends were the

207
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:18,417
most vicious of the three
major monster factions.

208
00:11:18,500 --> 00:11:21,457
If the frog fiend population's
been increasing lately,

209
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:25,217
wouldn't they be happy since it means
they could more easily fill their bellies?

210
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:28,317
That's because of the king frog
fiend that recently popped up.

211
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:33,282
In addition to being absurdly powerful in
battle, they're also exceptional leaders.

212
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:36,892
Small groups and lone wolves
alike tend to gather to them.

213
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:40,537
No wonder we had to be so
careful in dealing with them.

214
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:44,157
If it's not a big group, I don't
see why we can't just leave them be.

215
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:47,217
Captain, need I remind you
that they're carnivorous?

216
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:53,360
What do you think they'll do to satisfy
their hunger? Right. Humans, huh? Dang. Huh?

217
00:11:54,040 --> 00:11:57,557
Still, though, the purpose of this
mission was to gather information.

218
00:11:57,640 --> 00:11:59,837
We shouldn't go out of
our way to kill them.

219
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:02,637
But Crocodile Fiend
materials fetch a high price.

220
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:05,057
Now's our chance while
they're all starving and weak.

221
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:08,417
The Vice Captain completely
changes whenever money's involved.

222
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:11,437
Yeah, she's usually so
level-headed about everything.

223
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:14,957
I didn't know Vice Captain
Filmina was that kind of person.

224
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,864
Wait, just look at her captain.

225
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:19,218
I bet they're always short on money.

226
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:21,640
Fine, then we'll go put them down.

227
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,977
We'll launch our attack in
the middle of the night.

228
00:12:24,060 --> 00:12:26,060
Actually, I'd advise against that.

229
00:12:26,520 --> 00:12:28,137
Crocodile fiends are nocturnal.

230
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:30,102
They're more ferocious at night.

231
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:31,910
Oh, really?

232
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,640
We are on the same page.

233
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:36,350
All right, then.

234
00:12:36,433 --> 00:12:39,677
I want everyone to get plenty of rest
tonight, and we'll move out in the morning.

235
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:41,217
I'm counting on all of you.

236
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:42,130
Yeah!

237
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:55,277
Once the fighting starts,
I'll have nothing to do.

238
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:57,184
Lamas, don't do anything risky.

239
00:12:58,320 --> 00:13:02,120
And you, if things get
bad, protect Lamas for me.

240
00:13:02,960 --> 00:13:03,790
Hello there.

241
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:06,280
You've got my back? Thank you.

242
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:10,076
I wish I could do more to
assist you during the fight.

243
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:13,282
I've been racking my brain
for ways I could help.

244
00:13:14,440 --> 00:13:15,520
What's up, Boxo?

245
00:13:15,680 --> 00:13:17,915
You changed up the way you look again.

246
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,670
What's this?

247
00:13:23,753 --> 00:13:25,460
Whoa, it's cold!

248
00:13:26,320 --> 00:13:27,860
You mean this is ice?

249
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:31,680
But why would Voxo spit
out these cubes of ice?

250
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:34,897
I think he's telling us to
use it in the crocodile hunt.

251
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:35,810
Huh?

252
00:13:35,893 --> 00:13:36,723
Hello there!

253
00:13:37,060 --> 00:13:40,942
I see, but you'd have to be able
to dispense a ton of ice at once.

254
00:13:41,540 --> 00:13:42,370
Hello there!

255
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:44,640
Hmm, that's good to hear.

256
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:46,977
Tomorrow's battle is gonna be interesting.

257
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:48,537
You could even win a reward!

258
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,477
Hulemy, you're not making sense!

259
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:52,360
Tell me so I understand, too!

260
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:57,570
Captain!

261
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,906
The crocodile fiends
have finally come ashore!

262
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,473
They were shivering like they were cold!

263
00:14:03,640 --> 00:14:04,470
Excellent.

264
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:08,180
Seems everything's going
according to plan. And now,

265
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:12,617
we'll need a way to obstruct our view so
we can get closer without being noticed.

266
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:15,957
Covering the whole marsh with
fog magic will be too hard.

267
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:17,452
Well, if that's a no-go,

268
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:20,546
maybe we could try
spreading them into groups?

269
00:14:21,940 --> 00:14:23,240
What's going on, Boxo?

270
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:25,910
That's new.

271
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,708
What kind of shape is this?

272
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:30,600
What's that?

273
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:32,600
It's too cloudy to be ice.

274
00:14:32,940 --> 00:14:36,060
Are you making a new type
of hardened snow? Too bad.

275
00:14:37,360 --> 00:14:40,831
Captain, I think maybe he's
trying to say don't touch that.

276
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:44,496
Perhaps it's dangerous to
touch it without protection.

277
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:45,460
Hello there.

278
00:14:45,780 --> 00:14:47,200
Oh, thanks.

279
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:49,980
Look at that.

280
00:14:50,260 --> 00:14:52,037
That stuff's creating a bunch of fog.

281
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:54,217
You're just full of surprises, aren't you?

282
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:58,637
If we combine this with my magic, we
can obscure the entire area with fog.

283
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,367
That's a really clever idea.

284
00:15:00,680 --> 00:15:03,197
I knew I'd pick the right
magic item for this job.

285
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:05,927
You're trying to steal
credit again, Captain.

286
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:13,277
Honestly, stop your moping
and give us our orders.

287
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:16,557
Just go and pick them off one by
one like we discussed last night.

288
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,837
Your useless Captain's gonna
sit here and help himself

289
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:22,214
to sweeten tea while you deal
with the crocodile fiends.

290
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:25,440
Well, uh, I kind of want to go, too.

291
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:29,237
But Voxo has to stay and keep dumping
that stuff to keep the fog going.

292
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:31,217
Will you guys be okay without me?

293
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:32,130
Hello there!

294
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:34,420
Of course, we'll both be fine.

295
00:15:34,740 --> 00:15:38,040
I'm actually more worried
about you out there. Got it!

296
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:39,850
See ya!

297
00:15:39,933 --> 00:15:41,457
We'll be back before you know it!

298
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:42,370
Bye!

299
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:47,017
Well, everyone in the Menagerie
of Fools is an experienced hunter,

300
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:50,100
so I highly doubt they'll
do anything too reckless.

301
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,137
This works out.

302
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:53,220
I wanted to talk to you for a bit.

303
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:54,270
Hello there!

304
00:15:54,720 --> 00:15:58,757
As I said before, Director Bear
asked me to come along with you guys.

305
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:00,428
But my mission's different.

306
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:02,737
He wanted me to try to
figure out why things have

307
00:16:02,820 --> 00:16:05,702
started to go awry in the
Clearflow Lake Stratum.

308
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:07,737
I'm not sure if you know this or not,

309
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:11,055
but in each stratum there
exists a being called a lord.

310
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:15,460
They appear only on rare occasions,
and nobody knows what triggers it.

311
00:16:16,080 --> 00:16:18,962
Years or even decades can
pass between sightings.

312
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:21,060
It must be the dungeon boss.

313
00:16:21,220 --> 00:16:23,926
Kind of like the ones
you see in a video game.

314
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:25,010
Anyway,

315
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:29,397
seems the director thinks these disturbances
might be caused by the Lord's revival.

316
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:30,310
Hello there!

317
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:34,217
Did you know there's a rumor that
if you manage to defeat a Lord,

318
00:16:34,300 --> 00:16:36,697
you'll be bestowed with
an incredible treasure?

319
00:16:36,780 --> 00:16:41,545
Well, even if it is true, there's no way
we could take down the Lord of Estratum.

320
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:43,930
Huh?

321
00:16:44,013 --> 00:16:44,843
What's going on?

322
00:16:46,540 --> 00:16:47,460
No way!

323
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,200
Are you kidding me?

324
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:00,851
The Lord's actually here?

325
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:03,890
Damn it.

326
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:06,177
Looks like there's even stratum split.

327
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:07,620
What does that mean?

328
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:11,697
I've never heard that phrase, but I can
tell right away it's something really bad.

329
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:12,610
Where's Lama?

330
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:14,257
She's in the back, knocked down.

331
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:15,170
Kill me!

332
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:16,620
Drop all of my hands!

333
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:18,320
But what about Voxo?

334
00:17:18,420 --> 00:17:20,244
I'm not gonna leave him behind.

335
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:22,430
Poxo!

336
00:17:22,513 --> 00:17:23,498
What are you doing?

337
00:17:27,040 --> 00:17:27,960
Sorry, buddy.

338
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:30,259
We'll come back for you, I promise!

339
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,185
Get your damn hands off of me!

340
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:33,870
Poxo!

341
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:36,098
I look forward to serving you again.

342
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:38,230
Okay.

343
00:17:38,313 --> 00:17:39,240
Form change!

344
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:48,920
Raise durability by 100 to 200,

345
00:17:49,220 --> 00:17:53,926
raise toughness by 30 to 50, though it
might not be enough to make a difference.

346
00:17:58,560 --> 00:18:00,520
Points reduced by 1,000.

347
00:18:00,840 --> 00:18:01,700
1,000?

348
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:06,377
If I get hit with an attack stronger than
the barrier, it uses up a ton of points.

349
00:18:06,460 --> 00:18:10,177
If that thing hit me directly, I
would have been turned into scrap.

350
00:18:10,260 --> 00:18:14,731
But that's all the more reason I can't
let this big guy go after the others.

351
00:18:19,340 --> 00:18:22,752
I'll use the barrier to expel
these fried chicken lunches.

352
00:18:29,620 --> 00:18:30,450
Great.

353
00:18:30,533 --> 00:18:31,617
Seems it likes them.

354
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:33,940
In that case, eat on up!

355
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:36,400
I'll feed you until you explode!

356
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:40,620
Hello there!

357
00:18:54,600 --> 00:18:55,430
I'm alive.

358
00:18:59,420 --> 00:19:01,160
This has to be its stomach.

359
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:05,437
Whoa, my points are dropping like crazy!

360
00:19:05,520 --> 00:19:07,297
That means I don't have much time.

361
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:08,615
I better get to work.

362
00:19:09,080 --> 00:19:11,315
I'll create as much chaos as possible.

363
00:19:16,220 --> 00:19:17,580
Barrier ejection time!

364
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:20,200
Look at those babies fly!

365
00:19:20,740 --> 00:19:23,093
I'll give your stomach a good cleansing.

366
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:30,177
Oh, I guess that means it's working.

367
00:19:30,260 --> 00:19:32,117
Too bad it'll only give it a stomach ache.

368
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:34,082
I can't finish it off like that!

369
00:19:36,740 --> 00:19:41,097
Let's try one of those old gas vending
machines you'd sometimes see around old ends.

370
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:42,857
I've got an idea that might work.

371
00:19:42,940 --> 00:19:45,177
First, I'll fill up the barrier with gas.

372
00:19:45,260 --> 00:19:49,201
Then, when the pressure's built
up, I'll let it escape all at once.

373
00:19:54,100 --> 00:19:55,394
I need to make a fire.

374
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:59,557
I'll change into a model that has
the ability to warm up frozen food.

375
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:03,052
Then, restock an item directly
into my internal microwave.

376
00:20:03,860 --> 00:20:05,737
But I've never tried to do
something like that before.

377
00:20:05,820 --> 00:20:08,097
I'm not even sure I can
actually pull it off.

378
00:20:08,180 --> 00:20:09,637
This bending machine is my body.

379
00:20:09,720 --> 00:20:11,955
Now I've had months to get used to it.

380
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:13,757
I can do this.

381
00:20:13,840 --> 00:20:14,670
No.

382
00:20:14,753 --> 00:20:16,117
I have to do it.

383
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:17,717
Yes.

384
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:20,859
I'll do the same thing with
a towel and a newspaper.

385
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:24,960
And now the forbidden step.

386
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:29,335
Heating up a metal can in a microwave.

387
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:39,300
10 damage.

388
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:42,320
Durability has been
decreased by 10. Finally!

389
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:46,072
I'll use the barrier to toss
these items out into the gas.

390
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:49,780
I look forward to your next use.

391
00:21:06,820 --> 00:21:07,650
Owie!

392
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:11,130
Where'd it go?

393
00:21:12,060 --> 00:21:12,890
Hold on.

394
00:21:13,180 --> 00:21:16,457
These bones kind of look like
they belong to that thing.

395
00:21:16,540 --> 00:21:17,370
Oh!

396
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:25,300
This coin?

397
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:28,617
Could it be the incredible
treasure Hulemy was talking about?

398
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:30,406
I might as well take it then.

399
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:31,670
Huh?

400
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:33,940
Oh, crap. Wait a minute.

401
00:21:34,220 --> 00:21:36,200
Is this that stratum split thing?

402
00:21:36,380 --> 00:21:37,321
Oh, this is bad.

403
00:21:37,540 --> 00:21:39,957
Please, someone with the
blessing of might, save me!

404
00:21:40,040 --> 00:21:41,317
I mean, you don't have to have a blessing.

405
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:45,224
I'll take anyone strong enough to
carry around a vending machine!

406
00:21:53,200 --> 00:21:58,100
As I plunged into the darkness,
an image came to my mind.

407
00:22:00,740 --> 00:22:02,040
A scene of llamas.

408
00:22:02,820 --> 00:22:03,650
Crying

409
00:22:45,620 --> 00:22:48,420
Thank you.

410
00:23:06,220 --> 00:23:07,760
Thank you.

411
00:23:35,240 --> 00:23:36,680
Thank you very much.

412
00:23:37,080 --> 00:23:39,198
I look forward to serving you again.
